A table schema.sql no longer makes would lose its rows: refused. No table
is new, so the rename step's new name is left for the reader.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `menu` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its rows would go. Renamed? Add the step to ledger.sql: `ALTER TABLE menu RENAME TO <new name>;` Gone on purpose? `DROP TABLE menu;`
